# Web app folder structure (FSD, no barrels)

This project uses **Feature-Sliced Design** in `apps/web/src` with **direct imports only** — no `index.ts` barrel files.

## Top-level layout

```txt
apps/web/src/
  routes/          # TanStack Router file routes (thin wiring only)
  shared/          # Cross-cutting infrastructure and UI primitives
  features/        # Domain slices (auth, home, dashboard, …)
  views/           # Page-level composition components
  router.tsx       # Router factory
```

## Routes (`src/routes/**`)

- TanStack Router file routes live here (including `api/` and layout routes).
- Route files define `Route` with `createFileRoute` / `createRootRouteWithContext` only.
- **Delegate UI to `views`**, data/auth guards to `features` or `shared`.
- Do not put business logic, forms, or large JSX blocks in route files.

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD – routes/login.tsx
import { createFileRoute } from "@tanstack/react-router";
import { LoginView } from "@/views/auth/login-view";

export const Route = createFileRoute("/login")({
  component: LoginView,
});
```

## Shared (`src/shared/**`)

Move reusable, cross-domain code here:

- `shared/api/` — oRPC client, query client setup, TanStack Query utils.
- `shared/lib/` — auth client, small pure helpers, server-fn helpers when shared.
- `shared/middleware/` — generic middleware (auth, logging hooks).
- `shared/ui/` — app shell pieces (header, loader) and local wrappers around `@autolab/ui`.
- `shared/styles/` — global CSS (`index.css`).

**Do not** add domain-specific forms or page layouts to `shared`.

## Features (`src/features/<domain>/**`)

Each domain gets its own folder with **segments** (no barrel exports):

- `ui/` — presentational / interactive components (`sign-in-form.tsx`, `user-menu.tsx`).
- `lib/` — constants, validation, hooks, server functions for that domain.
- `model/` — optional local types/state when not shared.

Examples: `features/auth/`, `features/home/`, `features/dashboard/`.

When the same helper appears in 2+ features, promote it to `shared/lib/` or `shared/ui/`.

## Views (`src/views/<domain>/**`)

Page containers that wire features together:

- Naming: `<name>-view.tsx` exporting `<Name>View` (e.g. `home-view.tsx` → `HomeView`).
- Views orchestrate features + shared UI; keep domain logic in `features`.
- One view per primary route/page when practical.

## Backend API (`packages/api`)

All backend logic lives in `@autolab/api`, not in the web app. See `technologies/rpc/server-structure.mdc`.

## Imports

- Use `@/*` path alias with **explicit file paths**:
  - `@/shared/api/orpc`
  - `@/features/auth/ui/sign-in-form`
  - `@/views/home/home-view`
- **Never** import from folder barrels (`@/features/auth`, `@/shared/lib`) — those folders must not contain `index.ts` re-export files.

## What not to do

- No `src/app/` Next-style folder — routing is `src/routes/`.
- No `src/components/`, `src/lib/`, `src/utils/` at the root — use `shared/` or `features/`.
- No barrel `index.ts` files in FSD layers.
